<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syarif Muhammad Alkadrie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Syarif Muhammad Alkadrie was sultan of Pontianak in West Kalimantan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, from 1895 until his death in 1944. His long reign under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule saw the growth of Pontianak as a trading town. During the Japanese occupation he was arrested with other West Bornean leaders and executed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandor-affair">Mandor affair</a>; his son Hamid II later became sultan.</p></div>
